{"track":"tahsili","num":"8.01","title":"Exponentials & Logarithms","sections":[{"heading":"Evaluating exponential expressions","questions":[{"q":"Evaluate $2^5$.","answer":"$2^5=32$."},{"q":"Evaluate $3^{-2}$.","answer":"$3^{-2}=\\dfrac{1}{9}$."},{"q":"Evaluate $16^{1/2}$.","answer":"$16^{1/2}=4$."},{"q":"Evaluate $27^{2/3}$.","answer":"$27^{2/3}=(27^{1/3})^2=3^2=9$."}]},{"heading":"Evaluating logarithms","questions":[{"q":"Evaluate $\\log_2 32$.","answer":"Since $2^5=32$, $\\log_2 32=5$."},{"q":"Evaluate $\\log_3 81$.","answer":"Since $3^4=81$, $\\log_3 81=4$."},{"q":"Evaluate $\\log_5 1$.","answer":"$\\log_5 1=0$."},{"q":"Evaluate $\\log_{10} 0.01$.","answer":"Since $10^{-2}=0.01$, $\\log_{10}0.01=-2$."}]},{"heading":"Log laws: product and quotient","questions":[{"q":"Write $\\log_2(8x)$ as a sum of logarithms.","answer":"$\\log_2(8x)=\\log_2 8+\\log_2 x=3+\\log_2 x$."},{"q":"Write $\\log_3\\left(\\dfrac{x}{9}\\right)$ as a difference of logarithms.","answer":"$\\log_3\\left(\\dfrac{x}{9}\\right)=\\log_3 x-\\log_3 9=\\log_3 x-2$."},{"q":"Combine $\\log_5 5+\\log_5 25$ into a single logarithm and evaluate.","answer":"$\\log_5(5\\times25)=\\log_5 125=3$ (since $5^3=125$)."},{"q":"Combine $\\log_2 24-\\log_2 3$ into a single logarithm and evaluate.","answer":"$\\log_2\\left(\\dfrac{24}{3}\\right)=\\log_2 8=3$."}]},{"heading":"Log laws: the power rule","questions":[{"q":"Write $\\log(x^5)$ using the power rule.","answer":"$\\log(x^5)=5\\log x$."},{"q":"Evaluate $\\log_2(4^3)$ using the power rule.","answer":"$\\log_2(4^3)=3\\log_2 4=3(2)=6$."},{"q":"Write $2\\log_3 x+\\log_3 y$ as a single logarithm.","answer":"$2\\log_3 x+\\log_3 y=\\log_3(x^2y)$."}]},{"heading":"Expanding and condensing logarithmic expressions","questions":[{"q":"Expand $\\log\\left(\\dfrac{x^3y}{z^2}\\right)$ fully.","answer":"$3\\log x+\\log y-2\\log z$."},{"q":"Condense $3\\ln x-2\\ln y$ into a single logarithm.","answer":"$\\ln\\left(\\dfrac{x^3}{y^2}\\right)$."},{"q":"Expand $\\log_2\\left(\\sqrt{x}\\cdot y^3\\right)$ fully.","answer":"$\\sqrt{x}=x^{1/2}$, so the expression equals $\\dfrac{1}{2}\\log_2 x+3\\log_2 y$."}]},{"heading":"Solving exponential equations (matching bases)","questions":[{"q":"Solve $2^x=32$.","answer":"$32=2^5$, so $x=5$."},{"q":"Solve $3^{x+1}=81$.","answer":"$81=3^4$, so $x+1=4\\Rightarrow x=3$."},{"q":"Solve $5^{2x}=125$.","answer":"$125=5^3$, so $2x=3\\Rightarrow x=\\dfrac{3}{2}$."}]},{"heading":"Solving exponential equations using logarithms","questions":[{"q":"Solve $2^x=10$ for $x$, rounded to three decimal places.","answer":"$x=\\dfrac{\\log10}{\\log2}\\approx\\dfrac{1}{0.301}\\approx3.322$."},{"q":"Solve $5^x=40$ for $x$, rounded to three decimal places.","answer":"$x=\\dfrac{\\log40}{\\log5}\\approx\\dfrac{1.602}{0.699}\\approx2.292$."},{"q":"Solve $3^{2x}=50$ for $x$, rounded to three decimal places.","answer":"$2x=\\dfrac{\\log50}{\\log3}\\approx\\dfrac{1.699}{0.477}\\approx3.561$, so $x\\approx1.781$."},{"q":"Solve $e^x=15$ for $x$, rounded to three decimal places.","answer":"$x=\\ln15\\approx2.708$."}]},{"heading":"Solving logarithmic equations","questions":[{"q":"Solve $\\log_2(x)=5$.","answer":"$x=2^5=32$."},{"q":"Solve $\\log_3(x-1)=2$.","answer":"$x-1=3^2=9\\Rightarrow x=10$."},{"q":"Solve $\\log(x)+\\log(x-3)=1$.","answer":"$\\log[x(x-3)]=1\\Rightarrow x(x-3)=10\\Rightarrow x^2-3x-10=0\\Rightarrow(x-5)(x+2)=0$. Reject $x=-2$ (logarithm undefined); $x=5$."},{"q":"Solve $\\log_2(x+3)+\\log_2(x-1)=5$.","answer":"$\\log_2[(x+3)(x-1)]=5\\Rightarrow(x+3)(x-1)=32\\Rightarrow x^2+2x-35=0\\Rightarrow(x+7)(x-5)=0$. Reject $x=-7$ (makes $x-1<0$); $x=5$."}]},{"heading":"Natural logarithms and e","questions":[{"q":"Evaluate $\\ln(e^3)$.","answer":"$\\ln(e^3)=3$."},{"q":"Evaluate $\\ln(1)$.","answer":"$\\ln(1)=0$."},{"q":"Solve $\\ln(x)=2$ for $x$, in terms of $e$.","answer":"$x=e^2$."}]},{"heading":"Exponential growth and decay models","questions":[{"q":"The population of a town is modeled by $P(t)=5000e^{0.03t}$, where $t$ is in years. Find $P(10)$, rounded to the nearest whole number.","figure":{"type":"plot","fns":["5000*exp(0.03*x)"],"xmin":0,"xmax":30,"ymin":0,"ymax":13000,"width":220},"answer":"$P(10)=5000e^{0.3}=5000(1.34986)\\approx6749$."},{"q":"A radioactive substance decays according to $A(t)=200e^{-0.05t}$ (grams). Find $A(20)$, rounded to one decimal place.","answer":"$A(20)=200e^{-1}=200(0.36788)\\approx73.6$ grams."},{"q":"Determine whether $N(t)=50e^{0.02t}$ models growth or decay, and justify your answer.","answer":"Growth — the exponent's coefficient $0.02$ is positive, so $N$ increases as $t$ increases."}]},{"heading":"Word problems: exponential models in context","questions":[{"q":"This question has two parts. An investment of $2000$ dollars grows according to $A(t)=2000e^{0.04t}$, where $t$ is in years.","parts":["Find the value of the investment after $5$ years, rounded to the nearest dollar.","Find how many years it takes for the investment to double, rounded to one decimal place (using $\\ln2\\approx0.693$)."],"answers":["$A(5)=2000e^{0.2}=2000(1.2214)\\approx2443$ dollars.","$2=e^{0.04t}\\Rightarrow0.04t=\\ln2\\approx0.693\\Rightarrow t\\approx17.3$ years."]},{"q":"This question has two parts. A cup of coffee cools according to $T(t)=20+60e^{-0.1t}$ (°C), where $t$ is minutes after brewing and $20$°C is room temperature.","parts":["Find the temperature after $15$ minutes, rounded to one decimal place (using $e^{-1.5}\\approx0.2231$).","Find how many minutes it takes for the temperature to drop to $35$°C, rounded to one decimal place (using $\\ln4\\approx1.386$)."],"answers":["$T(15)=20+60e^{-1.5}=20+60(0.2231)\\approx33.4$°C.","$35=20+60e^{-0.1t}\\Rightarrow e^{-0.1t}=0.25\\Rightarrow-0.1t=-\\ln4\\approx-1.386\\Rightarrow t\\approx13.9$ minutes."]}]},{"heading":"MCQ — Evaluating exponential expressions","questions":[{"q":"Evaluate $3^4$.","choices":["$81$","$243$","$12$","$64$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$3^4=81$."},{"q":"Evaluate $4^{-2}$.","choices":["$-\\dfrac{1}{16}$","$\\dfrac{1}{16}$","$\\dfrac{1}{8}$","$16$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$4^{-2}=\\dfrac{1}{4^2}=\\dfrac{1}{16}$."},{"q":"Evaluate $25^{1/2}$.","choices":["$5$","$50$","$12.5$","$625$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$25^{1/2}=\\sqrt{25}=5$."},{"q":"Evaluate $8^{2/3}$.","choices":["$5.33$","$4$","$2$","$16$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$8^{2/3}=(8^{1/3})^2=2^2=4$."},{"q":"Evaluate $2^{-3}$.","choices":["$-8$","$\\dfrac{1}{6}$","$8$","$\\dfrac{1}{8}$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$2^{-3}=\\dfrac{1}{2^3}=\\dfrac{1}{8}$."},{"q":"Evaluate $32^{3/5}$.","choices":["$2$","$16$","$8$","$32$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$32^{3/5}=(32^{1/5})^3=2^3=8$."}]},{"heading":"MCQ — Evaluating logarithms","questions":[{"q":"Evaluate $\\log_3 27$.","choices":["$3$","$1$","$27$","$9$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$3^3=27$."},{"q":"Evaluate $\\log_2 64$.","choices":["$32$","$8$","$5$","$6$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$2^6=64$."},{"q":"Evaluate $\\log_7 1$.","choices":["$1$","Undefined","$7$","$0$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$7^0=1$."},{"q":"Evaluate $\\log_{10}0.001$.","choices":["$0.001$","$-3$","$-2$","$3$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$10^{-3}=0.001$."},{"q":"Evaluate $\\log_4 16$.","choices":["$4$","$8$","$2$","$16$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$4^2=16$."},{"q":"Evaluate $\\log_5 125$.","choices":["$5$","$3$","$1$","$25$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$5^3=125$."}]},{"heading":"MCQ — Log laws: product and quotient","questions":[{"q":"Write $\\log_3(9x)$ as a sum of logarithms.","choices":["$2+\\log_3 x$","$2\\log_3 x$","$9+\\log_3 x$","$\\log_3 9+\\log_3 x$ only"],"correct":0,"answer":"$\\log_3(9x)=\\log_3 9+\\log_3 x=2+\\log_3 x$."},{"q":"Write $\\log_5\\left(\\dfrac{x}{25}\\right)$ as a difference of logarithms.","choices":["$\\log_5 x-25$","$2-\\log_5 x$","$\\log_5 x-2$","$\\dfrac{\\log_5 x}{2}$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$\\log_5\\left(\\dfrac{x}{25}\\right)=\\log_5 x-\\log_5 25=\\log_5 x-2$."},{"q":"Combine $\\log_2 4+\\log_2 8$ into a single logarithm and evaluate.","choices":["$32$","$5$","$12$","$2$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$\\log_2(4\\times8)=\\log_2 32=5$."},{"q":"Combine $\\log_3 54-\\log_3 2$ into a single logarithm and evaluate.","choices":["$27$","$3$","$26$","$52$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$\\log_3(54\\div2)=\\log_3 27=3$."}]},{"heading":"MCQ — Log laws: the power rule","questions":[{"q":"Write $\\log(x^7)$ using the power rule.","choices":["$7\\log x$","$x^7\\log x$","$\\log x^7$ unchanged","$\\log(7x)$"],"correct":0,"answer":"Power rule: $\\log(x^n)=n\\log x$."},{"q":"Evaluate $\\log_3(9^2)$ using the power rule.","choices":["$18$","$81$","$2$","$4$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$2\\log_3 9=2(2)=4$."},{"q":"Write $3\\log_2 x+\\log_2 y$ as a single logarithm.","choices":["$3\\log_2(xy)$","$\\log_2(x^3+y)$","$\\log_2(x^3y)$","$\\log_2(3xy)$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$3\\log_2 x=\\log_2(x^3)$; combined with $\\log_2 y$: $\\log_2(x^3y)$."},{"q":"Write $4\\log x-\\log y$ as a single logarithm.","choices":["$\\log\\left(\\dfrac{x^4}{y}\\right)$","$\\log(4x-y)$","$4\\log\\left(\\dfrac{x}{y}\\right)$","$\\log\\left(\\dfrac{4x}{y}\\right)$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$4\\log x=\\log(x^4)$; combined: $\\log\\left(\\dfrac{x^4}{y}\\right)$."}]},{"heading":"MCQ — Expanding and condensing logarithmic expressions","questions":[{"q":"Expand $\\log\\left(\\dfrac{x^2y}{z^3}\\right)$ fully.","choices":["$2\\log x+\\log y-3\\log z$","$2\\log x-\\log y-3\\log z$","$\\log x^2+\\log y-\\log z^3$ unchanged","$2\\log x+\\log y+3\\log z$"],"correct":0,"answer":"Apply the quotient and power rules: $2\\log x+\\log y-3\\log z$."},{"q":"Condense $2\\ln x-3\\ln y$ into a single logarithm.","choices":["$\\ln\\left(\\dfrac{x^2}{y^3}\\right)$","$\\ln\\left(\\dfrac{x^2}{y}\\right)-3$","$\\ln\\left(\\dfrac{x^3}{y^2}\\right)$","$\\ln(x^2-y^3)$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$2\\ln x=\\ln(x^2)$, $3\\ln y=\\ln(y^3)$: $\\ln\\left(\\dfrac{x^2}{y^3}\\right)$."},{"q":"Expand $\\log_2\\left(\\sqrt{x}\\cdot y^4\\right)$ fully.","choices":["$\\dfrac{1}{2}\\log_2 x+4\\log_2 y$","$\\dfrac{1}{2}\\log_2 x+\\log_2 y^4$ unchanged","$2\\log_2 x+4\\log_2 y$","$\\dfrac{1}{4}\\log_2 x+2\\log_2 y$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$\\sqrt{x}=x^{1/2}$: $\\dfrac{1}{2}\\log_2 x+4\\log_2 y$."},{"q":"Condense $\\dfrac{1}{2}\\log x+2\\log y$ into a single logarithm.","choices":["$\\log(x\\cdot y^2)$","$\\log\\left(\\dfrac{\\sqrt{x}}{y^2}\\right)$","$\\log(\\sqrt{x}\\cdot y^2)$","$\\log(2\\sqrt{x}\\cdot y)$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$\\dfrac{1}{2}\\log x=\\log\\sqrt{x}$; combined: $\\log(\\sqrt{x}\\cdot y^2)$."}]},{"heading":"MCQ — Solving exponential equations (matching bases)","questions":[{"q":"Solve $2^x=64$.","choices":["$x=8$","$x=6$","$x=32$","$x=5$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$2^6=64$."},{"q":"Solve $3^{x+2}=27$.","choices":["$x=9$","$x=1$","$x=5$","$x=3$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$3^{x+2}=3^3\\Rightarrow x+2=3\\Rightarrow x=1$."},{"q":"Solve $5^{3x}=125$.","choices":["$x=\\dfrac{1}{3}$","$x=41.67$","$x=3$","$x=1$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$5^{3x}=5^3\\Rightarrow3x=3\\Rightarrow x=1$."},{"q":"Solve $4^x=\\dfrac{1}{16}$.","choices":["$x=4$","$x=-4$","$x=-2$","$x=2$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$4^x=4^{-2}\\Rightarrow x=-2$."},{"q":"Solve $2^{2x-1}=32$.","choices":["$x=3$","$x=2.5$","$x=6$","$x=5.5$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$2^{2x-1}=2^5\\Rightarrow2x-1=5\\Rightarrow x=3$."}]},{"heading":"MCQ — Solving exponential equations using logarithms","questions":[{"q":"Solve $2^x=12$ for $x$, rounded to three decimal places.","choices":["$3.585$","$3.170$","$4.000$","$2.485$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$x=\\dfrac{\\ln12}{\\ln2}\\approx3.585$."},{"q":"Solve $7^x=50$ for $x$, rounded to three decimal places.","choices":["$7.143$","$2.010$","$3.000$","$1.505$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$x=\\dfrac{\\ln50}{\\ln7}\\approx2.010$."},{"q":"Solve $4^{2x}=90$ for $x$, rounded to three decimal places.","choices":["$6.492$","$3.246$","$1.623$","$0.811$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$2x=\\dfrac{\\ln90}{\\ln4}\\approx3.246\\Rightarrow x\\approx1.623$."},{"q":"Solve $e^x=25$ for $x$, rounded to three decimal places.","choices":["$25.000$","$2.303$","$3.219$","$12.500$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$x=\\ln25\\approx3.219$."}]},{"heading":"MCQ — Solving logarithmic equations","questions":[{"q":"Solve $\\log_3(x)=4$.","choices":["$x=7$","$x=12$","$x=64$","$x=81$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$3^4=81$."},{"q":"Solve $\\log_2(x-1)=3$.","choices":["$x=6$","$x=9$","$x=7$","$x=8$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$x-1=2^3=8\\Rightarrow x=9$."},{"q":"Solve $\\log(x)+\\log(x-3)=1$.","choices":["$x=-2$","$x=5$","$x=10$","$x=13$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$\\log(x(x-3))=1\\Rightarrow x^2-3x-10=0\\Rightarrow(x-5)(x+2)=0$; only $x=5$ keeps both logs defined."},{"q":"Solve $\\log_2(x+2)+\\log_2(x-2)=5$.","choices":["$x=6$","$x=-6$","$x=34$","$x=18$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$(x+2)(x-2)=2^5=32\\Rightarrow x^2-4=32\\Rightarrow x^2=36$; only $x=6$ keeps both logs defined."}]},{"heading":"MCQ — Natural logarithms and e","questions":[{"q":"Evaluate $\\ln(e^5)$.","choices":["$0$","$e^5$","$1$","$5$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$\\ln(e^x)=x$."},{"q":"Evaluate $\\ln\\left(\\dfrac{1}{e}\\right)$.","choices":["$1$","$e$","$-1$","$0$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$\\ln(e^{-1})=-1$."},{"q":"Solve $\\ln(x)=3$ for $x$, in terms of $e$.","choices":["$x=e^{1/3}$","$x=3$","$x=e^3$","$x=3e$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$\\ln(x)=3\\Rightarrow x=e^3$."},{"q":"Evaluate $e^{\\ln7}$.","choices":["$7$","$\\ln7$","$1$","$e^7$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$e^{\\ln x}=x$."}]},{"heading":"MCQ — Exponential growth and decay models","questions":[{"q":"The population of a town is modeled by $P(t)=8{,}000e^{0.025t}$, where $t$ is in years. Find $P(15)$, rounded to the nearest whole number.","choices":["$8{,}300$","$11{,}000$","$11{,}640$","$12{,}000$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$P(15)=8{,}000e^{0.375}\\approx11{,}640$."},{"q":"A radioactive substance decays according to $A(t)=150e^{-0.04t}$ (grams). Find $A(25)$, rounded to one decimal place.","choices":["$60.7$","$50.0$","$75.0$","$55.2$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$A(25)=150e^{-1}\\approx55.2$ g."},{"q":"Determine whether $N(t)=80e^{-0.015t}$ models growth or decay.","choices":["Decay","Neither","Growth","Cannot be determined"],"correct":0,"answer":"The exponent's coefficient is negative: decay."},{"q":"Determine whether $M(t)=30e^{0.01t}$ models growth or decay.","choices":["Neither","Cannot be determined","Decay","Growth"],"correct":3,"answer":"The exponent's coefficient is positive: growth."},{"q":"The graph shows an exponential function. Based on the graph, does it represent growth or decay?","choices":["Neither","Growth","Cannot be determined","Decay"],"correct":1,"answer":"The curve rises as $x$ increases: growth.","figure":{"type":"plot","fns":["2**x"],"xmin":-2,"xmax":3,"ymin":0,"ymax":9}}]},{"heading":"MCQ — Word problems: exponential models in context","questions":[{"q":"An investment of 3,000 dollars grows according to $A(t)=3{,}000e^{0.05t}$ dollars, where $t$ is in years. Find the investment's value after 8 years, rounded to the nearest dollar.","choices":["$4{,}200$","$4{,}800$","$4{,}475$","$3{,}400$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$A(8)=3{,}000e^{0.4}\\approx4{,}475$ dollars."},{"q":"A cup of coffee cools according to $T(t)=22+70e^{-0.08t}$ (°C), where $t$ is in minutes. Find the temperature after 15 minutes, rounded to one decimal place.","choices":["$38.5^\\circ$C","$50.0^\\circ$C","$43.1^\\circ$C","$22.0^\\circ$C"],"correct":2,"answer":"$T(15)=22+70e^{-1.2}\\approx43.1^\\circ$C."},{"q":"A population of bacteria doubles every 3 hours, starting at 500. Using $P(t)=500\\cdot2^{t/3}$, find the population after 9 hours.","choices":["$4{,}000$","$2{,}000$","$8{,}000$","$1{,}500$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$P(9)=500\\times2^3=4{,}000$."},{"q":"The value of a car depreciates according to $V(t)=25{,}000(0.85)^t$ dollars, where $t$ is in years. Find the car's value after 5 years, rounded to the nearest dollar.","choices":["$11{,}093$","$12{,}750$","$9{,}500$","$10{,}625$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$V(5)=25{,}000(0.85)^5\\approx11{,}093$ dollars."}]}]}